<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Essen Cathedral</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essen">Essen</a> Cathedral is the cathedral of the Roman Catholic diocese of Essen in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhr">Ruhr</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It was built as the church of Essen Abbey, a community of noble canonesses founded in the 9th century, and keeps its Ottonian westwork and a Gothic hall church. It became a cathedral when the diocese was founded in 1958, and its treasury holds the Golden Madonna and other masterpieces of Ottonian art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/essen-cathedral.jpg" alt="Essen Cathedral" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gryffindor; derivative work by Hic et nunc · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Essen_2011_66-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
